          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Equivariant K-theory
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
          %p
            To the extent that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            is given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundles"} virtual vector bundles
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"}> topological K-theory
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+bundles"} equivariant bundles
            or generalizations to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
            thereof, as in
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+operator+K-theory"} equivariant operator K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+KK-theory"} equivariant KK-theory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#BottPeriodicity Bott periodicity
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+periodicity"} Bott periodicity
            of plain K-theory generalizes to equivariant K-theory:
          %p
            Complex equivariant K-theory is invariant under smashing with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+spheres"} representation spheres
            of complex representations (
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah68"}> Atiyah 68, Theorem 4.3
            ), while real equivariant K-theory is invariant under smashing with representation spheres of real 8d reps with spin structure (
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah68"}> Atiyah 68, Theorem 6.1
            ).
          %p
            Review in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Karoubi05"} Karoubi 05, Section 5
          %h3#complex_orientation Complex orientation
          %p
            Equivariant complex K-theory is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} equivariant complex oriented cohomology theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Greenlees01"}> Greenlees 01, Sec. 10
            ).
